<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n5996" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caecĭlĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A kind of lizard</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 6, 17,
				1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 17,
			4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Veg. 4, 21, 1</span></i> (in <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 51,
				76, § 166</span></i>: caecus serpens); now Ital. cecella;
			Sard. cicigna.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A kind of lettuce</i>, <i><span class="en">Col. 10,
				190</span></i>; cf. Caecilius, II. B.</div>
